<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!-- HOTSPOT CONFIGURATION. THE FEATURE THIS WAS ADDED FOR IS WITHDRAWN.

	     It was added on 2026-08-16 for fast sync — joining the recorder's own access point.
	     That capability was withdrawn on 2026-08-20 (`b0b352f`) because the recorder's AP
	     drops a client about eight seconds after the WPA2 handshake completes: measured six
	     times at 7.8s, 8.03s, 8.1s, 8.1s and 8.28s, three of them after taking a real DHCP
	     lease, once with the file selection and begin-transfer already issued over Bluetooth
	     with the phone still attached. A twenty-minute recording is ~4.8 MB and does not
	     cross an eight-second link.

	     WHY THE KEY IS STILL HERE, WHICH IS A DECISION AND NOT AN OVERSIGHT. Removing an
	     entitlement is a SIGNING change: the provisioning profile must be regenerated, and a
	     profile/binary mismatch fails at signing rather than at runtime — debug simulator
	     builds are unsigned, so a local green says nothing about it. Ripping it out to tidy
	     up would risk the ship path for a capability nobody is using. It is left in place,
	     named as dead, pending a deliberate profile change. Nick's call, not a cleanup.

	     THE CODE CANNOT REACH IT. `RecorderShelfControlsGateTests` fails if anything under
	     `App/` names `NEHotspotConfiguration`, `PocketWiFiCommand` or
	     `performReferenceWiFiCommand` — so this key grants a permission the application layer
	     has no path to use. THE ENTITLEMENT IS NOT THE RE-ENTRY BAR; the measurement is.
	     Finding this key enabled is not evidence that fast sync is one wiring job away. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.HotspotConfiguration</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.goforgeit.foundryx</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
